  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The boundary lemma>

    \;

    <math|<wide|\<Gamma\>|\<bar\>><rsub|q>> was built to converge to the bare
    action: <math|\<mu\><rsub|q>\<to\>\<mu\><rsub|N>>,
    <math|\<Theta\><rsub|q>\<to\>0>, corrections integrated from
    <math|q=\<infty\>>.

    <\lemma*>
      <dueto|fixed <math|N>, constants depend on <math|N>>

      <\equation*>
        <around|\<\|\|\>|Y<rsub|q>-\<Phi\><rsub|\<infty\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p>>+<around|\<\|\|\>|q*Z<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p>>\<le\>C<rsub|N,p>*<space|0.17em>q<rsup|-1/2>,<space|2em><text|hence><space|2em>\<delta\><rsub|N,T,p>\<le\>C<rsub|N,p>*T<rsup|-1>.
      </equation*>
    </lemma*>

    <\itemize>
      <item>The field at resolution <math|q>:
      <math|\<Phi\><rsub|q>=C<rsub|q>*P<rsub|q>=<around|(|q-q<rsub|0>|)>*C<rsub|q>*\<Phi\><rsub|\<infty\>>+C<rsub|q>*B<rsub|q-q<rsub|0>>\<to\>\<Phi\><rsub|\<infty\>>>.

      <item><math|\<Phi\><rsub|q>=Y<rsub|q>+C<rsub|q>*D*<wide|\<Gamma\>|\<bar\>><rsub|q><around|(|Y<rsub|q>|)>>,
      so <math|Y<rsub|q>-\<Phi\><rsub|q>=O<around|(|q<rsup|-1>|)>> and
      <math|D*<wide|\<Gamma\>|\<bar\>><rsub|q><around|(|Y<rsub|q>|)>\<to\>D*V<rsub|N><around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|\<infty\>>|)>>.

      <item>Exact minus approximate coordinate identity:

      <\equation*>
        q*Z<rsub|q>=q*C<rsub|q>*<around*|[|D*<wide|\<Gamma\>|\<bar\>><rsub|q><around|(|Y<rsub|q>|)>-\<bbb-E\><rsub|q>*D*V<rsub|N><around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|\<infty\>>|)>|]>;
      </equation*>

      compare <math|\<bbb-E\><rsub|q>*G> with the <strong|observed>
      <math|G<rsup|0><rsub|q>=D*V<rsub|N><around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|q>|)>>:
      <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|\<bbb-E\><rsub|q>*G-G|\<\|\|\>>\<le\>2*<around|\<\|\|\>|G-G<rsup|0><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>>>.
    </itemize>

    No uniform estimate, no posterior concentration.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|UV stability>

    \;

    Let <math|T\<to\>\<infty\>> at fixed <math|N> (paths and
    <math|\<nu\><rsub|N>> do not depend on <math|T>; monotone convergence;
    <math|\<delta\><rsub|N,T,p>\<to\>0>). <strong|Only then> take
    <math|sup<rsub|N>>.

    <\theorem*>
      <dueto|UV stability>For <math|q<rsub|0>=q<rsub|0><around|(|\<gamma\>|)>>
      large,

      <\equation*>
        sup<rsub|N><around*|(|<around|\<\|\|\>|E<rsup|N><rsub|\<infty\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p>>+<around|\<\|\|\>|J<rsup|N><rsub|\<infty\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p>>|)>\<le\>C<rsub|\<gamma\>>*<around|(|1+p<rsup|5>|)>,<space|2em>sup<rsub|N>
        \<bbb-E\><around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsup|N><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|2><rsup|2>\<le\>C<rsub|\<gamma\>>*q<rsup|-5/2>,
      </equation*>

      and <math|sup<rsub|N> \<bbb-E\>*exp
      <around|{|c*<around|(|E<rsup|N><rsub|\<infty\>>+J<rsup|N><rsub|\<infty\>>|)><rsup|1/5>|}>\<less\>\<infty\>>.
    </theorem*>

    <\itemize>
      <item><math|C<rsub|N,p>> diverges with <math|N>: never take
      <math|sup<rsub|N>> of <math|C<rsub|N,p>/T>.

      <item>The force: <math|F<rsub|q>=\<bbb-E\><rsub|q>*<around|[|-D*V<rsub|N><around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|\<infty\>>|)>|]>=K<rsub|q>*Z<rsub|q>-D*<wide|\<Gamma\>|\<bar\>><rsub|q><around|(|Y<rsub|q>|)>>,
      the explicit force at the approximate forecast, corrected by
      <math|K<rsub|q>*Z<rsub|q>>.
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <vspace*|2.5cm>

    \;

    <with|font-size|1.6|font-series|bold|color|dark red|Compactness>

    <vspace|0.3cm>

    <with|color|dark grey|Lecture 7>

    \;
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Suprema by a maximum principle>

    \;

    Embed by cells <math|\<square\><rsub|x>>:
    <math|\<iota\><rsub|N>:H<rsub|N>\<to\>H=L<rsup|2><around|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|3>|)>>
    isometric, <math|j<rsub|N>=\<iota\><rsub|N><rsup|\<ast\>>>.

    <\lemma*>
      <dueto|supremum after closure, <math|\<varpi\>=<frac|3|8>>><math|\<cal-Y\><rsub|T>=sup<rsub|q>
      q<rsup|-\<varpi\>><around|\<\|\|\>|Y<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>>,
      <math|\<cal-X\><rsub|T>=sup<rsub|q>
      q<rsup|-\<varpi\>><around|\<\|\|\>|X<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>>:

      <\equation*>
        \<cal-Y\><rsub|T>\<le\>C*<around*|(|\<cal-X\><rsub|T>+q<rsub|0><rsup|-\<varpi\>>*\<gamma\><rsup|1/2>*E<rsub|T><rsup|1/2>|)>,<space|2em><around|\<\|\|\>|\<cal-X\><rsub|\<infty\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p>>\<le\>C*<sqrt|p>.
      </equation*>
    </lemma*>

    <\itemize>
      <item>Remove the backward forcing: <math|\<cal-H\><rsub|q>=C<rsub|q>*F<rsup|Z><rsub|q>>,
      <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|\<cal-H\><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>\<lesssim\>q<rsup|-1/4><around|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|Z><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|2>\<lesssim\>\<gamma\><rsup|1/2>*E<rsub|T><rsup|1/2>>.

      <item>At frozen <math|q>: <math|K<rsub|q>*U+<frac|\<gamma\>|3>*<around|(|U+d|)><rsup|3>=f>.
      Constants are super- and subsolutions: <strong|lattice maximum
      principle>.

      <item>The weight <math|q<rsup|-\<varpi\>>> absorbs the memory:
      <math|q<rsup|-1-\<varpi\>>*<big|int><rsub|q<rsub|0>><rsup|q>s<rsup|\<varpi\>>\<le\><around|(|1+\<varpi\>|)><rsup|-1>>.
    </itemize>

    Finite-resolution suprema have all moments uniformly in <math|N>; the
    terminal field is a distribution.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Regularity and the terminal field>

    <\with|font-size|0.9>
      \;

      <with|font-series|bold|Space.> <math|K<rsub|q>*V<rsub|q>=f<rsub|q>>
      with <math|\<bbb-E\>*<big|int><rsub|I><around|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>><rsub|2><rsup|2>\<le\>C<rsub|I>>
      (energies), so <math|V\<in\>L<rsup|2><around|(|I;H<rsup|1>|)>>;
      <math|Y=V+X-\<varrho\><around|(|Y|)>> has the regularity of the free
      field: <math|H<rsup|\<sigma\>>>, <math|\<sigma\>\<less\><frac|1|2>>, in
      space; <math|H<rsup|\<theta\>>>, <math|\<theta\>\<less\><frac|1|2>>, in
      scale; tight in space\Utime <math|L<rsup|p>> (and in
      <math|C*<around|(|I;H|)>>: <math|C<rsup|1/4>> Hölder bound <math|+>
      uniform Fourier tails).

      <with|font-series|bold|Terminal field.>
      <math|H<rsub|q><rsup|2>\<le\><frac|C|q>*C<rsub|q>> gives, for
      <math|<frac|1|2>\<less\>s\<less\><frac|3|2>>,

      <\equation*>
        <big|int><rsub|Q><rsup|\<infty\>><around|\<\|\|\>|<around|(|1-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|-s/2>*H<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|<math-up|HS>><rsup|2>\<mathd\>q\<le\>C*<big|int><rsub|Q><rsup|\<infty\>><frac|1|q>*<big|sum><rsub|k><frac|<around|(|1+<around|\||k|\|><rsup|2>|)><rsup|-s>|q+c<around|\||k|\|><rsup|2>>\<mathd\>q\<le\>C<rsub|s>*Q<rsup|-<around|(|s-<frac|1|2>|)>>,
      </equation*>

      and the drifts have squared tails <math|O<around|(|Q<rsup|-3>|)>>,
      <math|O<around|(|Q<rsup|-5/2>|)>>, <math|O<around|(|Q<rsup|-3/2>|)>>.
      Doob:

      <\equation*>
        sup<rsub|N> \<bbb-E\>*sup<rsub|t\<ge\>Q><around|\<\|\|\>|Y<rsub|t>-Y<rsub|Q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|H<rsup|-s>><rsup|2>\<le\>C<rsub|s>*Q<rsup|-<around|(|s-<frac|1|2>|)>>.
      </equation*>

      <\corollary*>
        <math|\<nu\><rsub|N>> is tight in
        <math|H<rsup|-s><around|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|3>|)>> for every
        <math|s\<gtr\><frac|1|2>>, with all moments uniformly in <math|N>.
        (Threshold of the free field in <math|d=3>.)
      </corollary*>
    </with>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
